STYLE: A grand hand-made toy theatre production built from printed card. Every piece is a flat cutout of thick card about 4 mm thick, cut by hand with a craft knife, with raw brown card at the edges. The face is painted in soft charcoal line and grey ink wash with thin watercolour on warm Korean hanji mulberry paper, its long fibres visible. Loose expressive charcoal strokes and quiet, tender faces. Broad, calm shapes readable from the back row. Puppet joints are round brass split pins. The present day has the last amber and persimmon light of dusk over indigo-grey water; the memories are cool and rain-washed. Palette: hanji cream #EDE6D6, charcoal #2B2A28, slate #5E6670, mist #C9CDD0, earth #6E5A44, indigo #3B4A66, pine #4E5E48, persimmon #B4553A, dusk amber #D6A365, raw card #A57E52. The mood is family love, regret and unanswered longing in Korea, many years after a separation in June 1950.
CONSTRAINTS: No text, writing, lettering, numbers, logos, signature or watermark. No national flags, insignia, emblems, armbands or badges. No violence or weapons in use. No real persons. No photographic people, plastic, glossy finish, anime style or sculpted 3D characters. The illustration must remain a painted, flat card cutout. The rods, strings, light and sky will be added by the theatre.
Use case: illustration-story.
Image 1 is the production's key-art STYLE reference. Match its charcoal, ink, thin watercolour, hanji fibres, raw card edges, palette and figure style. Do not copy its composition.
SUBJECT: The FOUR detached pieces of ONE elderly Cheol marionette, painted at one consistent scale, with at least 90 pixels of empty space between every piece. He faces three-quarters to the RIGHT. (1) A separate head with short WHITE hair, a lined strong kind Korean face, quiet sad eyes, and a bare neck with NO collar; one round brass pin at the bottom of the neck. (2) An ARMLESS and HEADLESS body from the neck base down to worn dark shoes: a worn grey-brown coat over a cream shirt, a faded indigo scarf draped down the chest, dark trousers, a slightly stooped standing pose. Three clearly visible round brass pins: neck base and both shoulders. (3) His RIGHT arm from shoulder to an open reaching hand, grey-brown coat sleeve, one brass shoulder pin. (4) His LEFT arm from shoulder to a hand holding a plain wooden walking cane extending down beside the hand, grey-brown sleeve, one brass shoulder pin. Do not put arms on the body. Do not let any pieces touch. Natural adult head-to-body proportions. Arrange head at upper left, body in centre, right arm at right, left arm at far left below the head. This is a production sprite-parts sheet, not an assembled character. Square image, 2048 pixels if possible.
Transparent sprite-parts sheet, front view. No shadows, rods, strings, scenery or lettering.
